{{!-- A2's lead: the publication states its newest story typographically, with no cover photo.

	{{> "home/masthead" feed=feed}}

The same first row of the same query A1 leads with — the difference between the two layouts is
the drawing, never the data.

A PUBLICATION WITH ONE WRITER DOES NOT SIGN ITS OWN HERO. The avatar and the byline are drawn
only once a second writer has published, which leaves the read time centred alone — and that is
partials/writers.hbs's rule, one Surface further down: "one chip under the word Writers states
what every byline on the page already said". Here it is the publication's own name, under the
publication's own name in the header. A publication with a masthead worth stating states it in
both places; a solo writer states it in neither.

The test is `writers.[1].count.posts` over `order="count.posts desc"`, which is writers.hbs's
too, and for its reason: count.posts is NOT filterable on authors in Ghost 6, and Handlebars
cannot compare a total to 2 — but the SECOND row of a descending order carries the second-highest
count, so if it has published then at least two writers have. `limit="2"` is all the test reads.

The query wraps the {{#foreach}} rather than sitting inside the section: `writers` is a block
param, so it stays in scope over the post context the foreach switches to, and every post field
below reads normally. Only the foreach's own argument is a parent path — `../feed`, one frame up
for the get.

The face is the writer's, at 32px, drawn by post/avatar.hbs so a publication whose writers
uploaded photos gets photos here as it does everywhere else.

NO RULE UNDER IT. The design closes this block with a border, which lands 24px above the rule
home/digest.hbs already draws over its own heading — two hairlines, one gap apart, neither
separating anything the other does not. The section keeps its bottom margin, so the spacing is
unchanged. --}}
{{#get "authors" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="2" as |writers|}}
	{{#foreach ../feed limit="1"}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="a2-lead"
			class="container pt-20 text-center">
			<p class="font-meta text-meta text-muted tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">
				{{~#primary_tag}}{{name}}<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>{{/primary_tag~}}
				{{date format="DD MMM YYYY"}}
			</p>

			<h1
				id="a2-lead"
				class="font-display tracking-display mt-6 text-[clamp(36px,4.6vw,60px)] leading-[1.08] font-medium text-balance">
				<a
					href="{{url}}"
					class="text-text no-underline">{{title}}</a>
			</h1>

			<p class="font-body text-muted mx-auto mt-[22px] max-w-[58ch] text-[21px] leading-[1.55] text-pretty italic">{{excerpt}}</p>

			<div class="mt-7 mb-11 flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
				{{#if writers.[1].count.posts}}
					{{#primary_author}}
						{{> "post/avatar" size="size-8" textSize="text-xs"}}
					{{/primary_author}}

					{{> "byline-links" linkClass="font-ui text-text text-sm font-semibold no-underline"}}
				{{/if}}

				<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{reading_time seconds=(t "< 1 min read") minute=(t "1 min read") minutes=(t "% min read")}}</span>
			</div>
		</section>
	{{/foreach}}
{{/get}}
